#glassblowing #chandelier #glassart', 'datetime': '2026-05-22T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '3902764715470260244', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-dfw5-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/705411859_18443317624141925_8415549696851761538_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=106&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0FST1VTRUxfSVRFTS5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=07mRO4wl1MwQ7kNvwH2c1Si&_nc_oc=AdoEnlrvjcf4oOrUrlOm2qFT09AlGdbWmWcOu242ug-MHmw3BRNpvrb_kfjLpE4Welk&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-dfw5-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=m_4NZPVqPHidPoLGjDSf2g&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQS2b8sWeSAYd_K5FHME0_23CWNGeptDBEx6jsjacEgV8Q&oe=6AED4FCB', 'post_hashtags': ['glassblowing', 'chandelier', 'glassart'], 'content_type': 'Carousel', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DYpZ9S7iIgU'}, {'caption': 'The attempt #5 glass pumpkin! 

It came in at 97 inches around. Which, if you don’t know off the top of your head, is the same as @corningmuseum giant glass pumpkin from 2009😅 sooo close! AHHH

It ended up weighing 46 pounds when we weighed it 2 days later. Officially the heaviest thing I have worked on. 

Thank you to the team! It went really smooth. 
